WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.810
The battle between England and France 
was about to climax at Orléans.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.910
If this land can be conquered,

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:13.780
the English army will be able 
to topple the rest of South France.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.620
On the other hand, 
if this land can be protected,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:22.550
the French army will be able to organize 
the crowning ceremony for Princess Charlotte.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.080
Montmorency was trying to command 
a troop of about one hundred soldiers

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.910
to deliver provisions to Orléans.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.260
However, the bridge used 
to cross the Loire River

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.170
was already occupied by the English army,

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:41.180
and the impregnable Tourelles complex
sits on the southern shore.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.230
A frontal assault will be difficult.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.360
It looks like our best option is to go around
 to the relatively unguarded east side,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.100
and carry our provisions across 
the upper Loire River using boats.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.410
Astaroth.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.130
Please tell the commanding officer in 
Orléans to bring over diversionary troops.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.270
Fine, fine.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.080
I almost wish I couldn't fly.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:29.270
<b>#06 Ashes to Ashes</b>

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.510
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.040
<b>Orléans Fortress</b>

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.470
Please carry them to the barn in the back.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.310
There's no rush.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.430
We're almost there! You can do it!

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.640
Montmorency.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.200
Oh, Batard.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.490
Long time, no see.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.220
The commanding officer was a princess knight?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.670
I'm male.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:34.440
My cousin, Princess Charlotte, has forced me 
to dress like a girl since I was a child.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.120
I don't need a little brother!

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.440
I want a little sister!

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.720
I see!

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.200
That's why your chest is flat!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.720
I don't like girls!

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.330
Charlotte bullied him 
all these years, after all.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.540
I'm not scared of gentlemen,

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.350
so you can touch me, Montmorency.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.660
Why would I want to touch you?!

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.010
Yet, your cheeks are turning red.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.740
Cut it out!

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.300
What a reckless bunch.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.220
I've heard rumors, but I wasn't expecting you
 to be walking around with an archangel.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.480
Who's that?

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.470
Alençon.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.630
Richemont's younger brother.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.980
My sister is so selfish!

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.000
Don't say that.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.230
She's a disgrace to knighthood.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:26.010
Oh, well. We now have a promising 
reinforcement instead.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.790
Leave it all to me!

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.600
He's being sarcastic. It's sarcasm.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.420
Huh?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.070
It's still not too late.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:34.750
Send her back to Domremy.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.090
What?!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.600
They're about to break our front line!

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.810
I'll head out.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.580
Do you understand, Montmorency?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.990
Throwing a shepherd girl 
dressed in armor into a battle

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.860
violates the code of chivalry!

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.580
Is it just me, or is he 
more stubborn than before?

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:57.020
It's not easy to have such 
an accomplished sister.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.690
<i>Think of this as an opportunity, Alençon.</i>

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.370
<i>If you change the tide of this battle 
on your own, now that your sister is gone,</i>

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.220
<i>no one will call you the 
useless little brother again.</i>

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.300
Fear not!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.800
Justice is on our side!

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.560
Therefore, God is also on our side!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.780
Get out of my way!

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.430
What?!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.330
<i>What was that?</i>

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.380
I shall be your opponent.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.880
<i>Are you telling me that 
she is that girl from before?</i>

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.740
Who are you?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.990
Ulysses Noire.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:32.590
Noire?

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.490
You call yourself the black Ulysses?

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.380
Interesting.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:41.000
the white Ulysses shall test 
your worthiness for that name!

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.770
<i>This is not a fight between human beings.</i>

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.530
I wanted to see you.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:05.410
I came here because 
I wanted to see you so badly!

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.950
We'll see how long you can keep laughing!

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.160
Too fast!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.810
You actually dodged my attack?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.600
Jeanne!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:46.820
Wait!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.920
Stop chasing!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.200
Don't forget that you can remain 
Ulysses for only three minutes!

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.380
Are you all right?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.910
Retreat!

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.400
I-Incredible!

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.700
She's a real saint?!

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.330
I can't believe it!

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:21.850
I never knew there was such 
a wonderful woman in the world!

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.040
Give her a handshake later, will you?

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.360
P-Please don't make me.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.870
<b>Paris</b>

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.920
Ulysses...

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.600
"Ulysse" in French, huh?

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.000
Overwhelming fighting power.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:56.240
However, England used to be
 a land of monsters.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:01.150
The history of battle for us is 
the history of monster hunting.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:03.530
This is nothing that we 
haven't encountered before.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.980
Isn't that right, Glasdale?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.750
It's gonna cost you.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.480
Not a problem.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.900
Money is no object.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:17.340
Hunt that unsightly monster for me!

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.180
Oops, "monster" was a bit too much.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:21.910
Forgive me.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:30.880
I hope you can refrain from 
acting on your own next time.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.880
We're a team.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:33.920
Yes.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.580
Our saint!

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.960
Maiden of Domremy!

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.000
The archangel is with them!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.240
I don't feel right about this...

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:51.280
I'm not a real savior.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.570
You're a savior in your own right.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.260
Really?

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:57.450
Then...

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.210
Thank you!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.490
Thank you!

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.450
Let's do our best together!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.890
I can't believe you took 
down a fortress so easily.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:12.360
The most important thing 
in war is the command.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:13.210
Also,

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:18.220
strong winds blow at specific times around 
the Loire River at this time of the season.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:21.720
Light up a fire, and before long...

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.870
This is France.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:25.800
We have geographical advantages.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.700
You're the best, Montmorency!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:29.850
Let go!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.960
I'm not into boys!

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.580
S-Sorry.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.270
I feel so rejuvenated!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.280
Y-You...

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:16.230
It's like I'm addicted to Montmorency now!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.200
I need more elixir!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.040
Give me more baiser!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.800
You've already had enough!

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.580
I still need more!

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:34.840
I can't produce more! No more!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.950
What's wrong with me?!

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.270
Montmorency,

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:00.400
you're starting to see 
Jeanne as the opposite sex

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.290
as you continue to baiser with her.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.480
She's just a child!

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.440
But you're still a male, and she's a female.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:12.040
The desire for procreation is 
the fundamental instinct of all animals.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.860
This is absolutely wrong.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.920
I must think of a solution right away!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.490
There is a solution.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.970
R-Really?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.150
Take out the Philosopher's Stone.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.450
Huh? Okay.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.230
This is...

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:40.870
If you can draw out the power 
of the Philosopher's Stone to its limit,

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:43.320
this beauty will be yours.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:47.780
The Philosopher's Stone 
still has a secret like that?

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.170
If you can embrace her with your hands,

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.290
you won't be interested in human girls again.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.420
I can't.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.510
She is, indeed, astonishingly beautiful,

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:07.050
but true love can't be born 
without spending time together.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.960
Just kidding.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:13.520
I read that from some novel.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.530
Astaroth?

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:27.620
No one has successfully obtained her yet.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:31.260
Heroes are all blinded 
by the radiant fires of war

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.040
and romance in front of them,

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:38.040
and they all forget about her.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.680
What's happening?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.310
The townspeople have gone out of control!

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:58.940
We won't let the English 
do as they like anymore!

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.000
We have a saint on our side!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.320
We can go to heaven if we die in battle!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.920
They headed to the Tourelles complex?

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.860
The English troops are 
all gathered in that fortress!

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.870
We don't have a strategy 
for defeating Ulysses Noire, either.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.670
Why didn't you stop them?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.920
No one would listen to me!

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.340
It's all your fault!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.090
What?

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.220
They're unable to take action
 if they're too demoralized,

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:30.800
but if they get too worked up, 
they become irrational and go out of control!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.020
You and the female saint boosted 
the townspeople's morale too much!

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.640
I'll take command.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:42.610
Any objections?

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.870
This will violate the code of chivalry,

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.720
but we'll use the mob headed for
 the Tourelles complex as a diversion,

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:51.270
and our forces will conquer the other fortresses.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:54.370
We cannot let them die in vain.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.490
<i>That's a very logical course of action.</i>

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:00.280
<i>Richemont didn't train him for nothing.</i>

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:02.380
We can't do that, Count Alençon.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.380
Jeanne.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:08.030
We have to head to the Tourelles complex, too!

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:10.620
We came all this way to save 
the people of Orléans,

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:14.510
but it would be pointless 
if we used them as a diversion!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.410
We don't have enough manpower 
for a frontal assault of a fortress

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:20.020
guarded by enemy forces.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.210
I'll go to the fortress, 
even if it means going alone.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:27.650
J-Jeanne, if you die, 
Orléans would truly be doomed!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.210
If that happens...

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.340
English troops that are excited after seeing 
blood in the battlefield would say...

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.560
"I don't care if he's a boy!"

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:35.990
then the English soldiers 
would push me down, and...

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.360
Mommy!

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.940
War requires strategy and discipline.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:47.000
If you let your emotions take over, 
we'll just get taken down one by one.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.850
No! No!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.420
Please, calm down, Jeanne.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.940
Jeanne's emotions are resonating 
with the stone inside her,

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.430
and it's on the verge of losing control.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.080
Astaroth...

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.660
Give it up.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.260
No one can stop her now.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.720
What a turn of events.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.710
Damn it!

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:28.890
Who would've thought they would 
come head-on without a strategy.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:31.260
They must be desperate.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:32.720
Oh, well.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:35.860
I'll just be doing my job.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.150
I'm sorry, Montmorency.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:44.730
"Let's ignore peasants who don't listen,
 and use them as a diversion!"

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:47.530
If you'd said that with a smile, 
it would've troubled me more.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.720
Waiting for the right time.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:50.410
Got it?

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.230
Okay.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:53.120
God bless the maiden!

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.120
Become human shields, heroes of Orléans!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.470
These are not the usual weak French peasants!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:03.990
The witch sucked their blood 
and now they're... immortal!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:08.000
Passion is overwhelming their fear.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.440
Just as Montmorency predicted... so far.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.510
Where's the Ulysses?

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.360
Glasdale.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.610
I'm William Glasdale!

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:22.670
Remember the name of the one 
who kills you before you die!

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:27.160
Witch, Ulysses, enemy of mankind!

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:32.280
Looks like you couldn't die, 
so I'll help turn you into ashes!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.540
They've finally shown up.

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:37.210
Yes. If the battle drags on,

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.620
the commanding officer will 
eventually show up at the front line.

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:41.500
Jeanne!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.110
Please run for cover!

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.040
Run for cover!

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.550
Go for it!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.560
What?!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.130
You're mine!

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.070
Jeanne!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:26.080
The power granted by your 
Philosopher's Stone is "acceleration."

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.750
But you can't accelerate while in free fall.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.210
That's the rule.

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:37.320
Glasdale's attack was a diversion,

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:40.750
to make you jump and 
initiate a free fall attack.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.880
So that I could capture you, like this.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.920
French girl.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.720
The first projectile was a fake.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.880
This is my real weapon...

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.180
Ash to ash!

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.480
No! That arrow is...

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:58.740
Let go!

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:04.490
This may the ideal ending for us.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.910
We can die while we're still pure.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:11.130
While being watched by 
our beloved Montmorency.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.250
Who are you?

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.060
Ashes to ashes.

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:18.810
Those who should die should 
head to realm of the dead.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.780
Die, Jeanne.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.200
As expected of monsters,

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.750
you're still alive and moving.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.250
But you know, this arrow...

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:50.580
is borrowed from the Holy Lance 
in Antioch that killed Jesus.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.080
It's a Philosopher's Stone!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:58.250
Even without drinking elixir, 
giving up my humanity...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:03.720
I can weild a Philosopher's Stone
 as a weapon and kill a Ulysses!

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:08.310
Ulysses can regenerate any part 
of the body other than the brain,

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:12.560
but organs taken by this weapon won't heal.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.280
The wielder of the Holy Lance

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:19.240
can hunt down monsters that should be 
exterminated from the world of mankind.

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:23.320
That's who I am, the Ulysses Hunter!

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:28.650
Eternal separation from Montmorency...

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:33.400
in other words, you fear death.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:37.530
Then there's me, who's waiting to die.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.710
I was no match for you from the start.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.840
Montmorency...

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.650
<i>Jeanne...</i>

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.350
Don't...

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.850
Montmorency...

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.180
Montmorency...

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.400
Montmorency...

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.560
Don't!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:15.520
Grab the witch's body!

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.300
Remove the Philosopher's Stone
 from her corpse!

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:23.210
The Duke of Bedford will generously 
reward anyone who gets it!

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.040
Our saint was killed...

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:27.000
It's over!

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.230
Montmorency, we have to retreat!

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:39.730
Hurry, Montmorency!

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.980
Get ahold of yourself, Montmorency!

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:46.250
Jeanne is...

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.310
dead.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:34.970
<b>#07 Rain and Memory in Brittany</b>

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:23.480
The most beautiful shape in nature...

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:26.400
is the shape of Étienne's breasts, 
which are about the same in height and width.

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:28.400
I call them the Golden Breasts.

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:30.830
Episode 7: Rain and Memory in Brittany

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:32.510
That has nothing to do with a preview,

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.800
but don't worry about it!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>"I never knew there was such 
a wonderful woman in the world!"</b>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Use it when you see a wonderful woman!</b>
